","cmd-d66c2b2b2f3f4180","cmd-322184d73e4d4565","cmd-635d110c029e44cb","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. node1 has an active LUKS2-backed XFS volume at /srv/secure, and a directly observed reboot proved automatic unlock, automatic mounting, and data persistence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service and data state are all captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots are generic and do not independently inspect /srv/secure or its configuration; those task-specific facts are established by direct executor command evidence instead."]}
